course: dictionary
lesson: 15096
title: Rotting and what it tells you
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Rotting means going bad and breaking down slowly. Dead leaves, old fruit and food rot when tiny living things break them down. «The old apple was rotting in the grass, brown and soft.» The words brown and soft are the clues: rotting is not a happy word, and the apple is going bad.
explain: Rotting can also describe wood and teeth that are slowly being damaged. «The rotting log was soft enough to push my finger into.» A good log is hard, so soft wood tells you it is rotting. Context helps you here: look for clues like soft, brown, smelly or weak.
explain: Sometimes rot is used for things that are left alone and get worse. «The bike was left rotting in the shed for years.» Nobody is breaking the bike on purpose; it is getting worse because nobody cares for it. Always ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it makes sense.
fact: Rotting means going bad and breaking down slowly.
fact: Bacteria, fungi and worms break down dead things, and this is called decomposition.
fact: In a compost heap, rotting leaves and peelings turn into rich soil that plants can use.
fact: Rotting food smells bad and must never be eaten.
fact: «Sugar can cause rotting teeth», so brush your teeth well and limit sweets.
exercise: «The old apple was rotting in the grass.» What does rotting mean here? | Shining brightly in the sun | *Going bad and breaking down | Being picked up by a child | Growing bigger and redder
exercise: In a compost heap, leaves and peelings are rotting. What is happening to them? | They are growing into trees straight away | They are freezing solid in the cold | *They are being broken down by tiny living things and turning into soil | They are being painted by the wind
exercise: «Do not eat the rotting fruit you find under the tree.» Why should you not eat it? | Because it is too sweet | Because it is too big to chew | *Because it has gone bad and may make you ill | Because it is cold inside
test: «The rotting log was soft enough to push my finger into.» What does rotting describe? | *Wood slowly going soft and breaking down | Wood that is brand new | Wood that is painted red | Wood that is very heavy and hard
test: A dentist says, «Sugar can cause rotting teeth.» What does rotting teeth mean? | Teeth that are shiny and white | Teeth that have fallen out on purpose | Teeth that are very long and sharp | *Teeth being slowly damaged and getting weak
exam: «The bike was left rotting in the shed for years.» What does rotting mean here? | Being moved to a new house | *Getting worse slowly because nobody cares for it | Growing fast in the sunshine | Being cleaned every single day
